  },
  "_types_documents": "One block per type of document. \"signaux\": words that identify the type (the most frequent wins). \"fin_entete\": headings, at the start of a line, that mark the end of the parties section. \"separateurs\": words, at the start of a line, that open a party's block without giving its role (BETWEEN, AND...). For each role: \"code\" (form of the tag), \"pluriel\" (true = numbered CLAIMANT1, CLAIMANT2; false = PROVIDER, then PROVIDER2 if there is a second one), \"qualites\" (words that designate this role in the parties section), \"ouvreurs\" (words, at the start of a line, that open this role's block).",
  "_definitions_roles_admis": "Defined terms of a contract (\"hereinafter the X\") accepted as a party code, IN ADDITION to the usual roles the program knows (Provider, Customer, Lessor, Lessee, Licensee...). Any other defined term (a name, an acronym, a brand: \"hereinafter \"AGICE\"\") is discarded: a tag must never reveal the name it masks. Add your own speciality roles here, in capitals.",
  "definitions_roles_admis": [],
